  "description": {
    "text": "Seven promos of the Pokémon Players Club, released in May 2007 and numbered 001/PPP to 007/PPP, with the club's logo as their symbol. Members earned them with experience points (EXP), under a system that made the prizes much easier to reach than the one of 2005: Turtwig, Chimchar and Piplup at 2,000 EXP, Manaphy at 3,000, Dialga at 5,000, Palkia at 7,000 and Darkrai at 10,000. Several hold items, and all came out in English in the Majestic Dawn expansion. In April 2008 the Pokémon Daisuki Club replaced the Players Club, and its Action Point system replaced EXP that November.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: PPP Promotional cards (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 4 August 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260804041215/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/PPP_Promotional_cards_(TCG)"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tell": {
